00:19:40.232 --> 00:19:43.041
- Now listen, success is a choice.

00:19:43.041 --> 00:19:45.712
It is a choice to do something.

00:19:45.712 --> 00:19:48.959
It's a decision, so if
you choose to do nothing,

00:19:48.959 --> 00:19:51.583
you'll be successful at that, nothing.

00:19:51.583 --> 00:19:54.410
But if you choose to take a
step in the right direction

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:58.995
and you'll be much, much closer
to achieving your dreams.

00:19:58.995 --> 00:20:00.985
So are you ready to take that step?

00:20:00.985 --> 00:20:03.969
This first step today to transform

00:20:03.969 --> 00:20:06.594
your life into a victorious life.

00:20:06.594 --> 00:20:09.417
I want you to take a piece of paper out

00:20:09.417 --> 00:20:11.647
and I want you to list the major projects

00:20:11.647 --> 00:20:15.602
that you want to fulfill in a year's time.

00:20:15.602 --> 00:20:18.682
I want you then to prioritize them,

00:20:18.682 --> 00:20:21.348
one, two, three, and four.

00:20:21.348 --> 00:20:23.045
Then I want you, over the course

00:20:23.045 --> 00:20:26.045
of three months, finish one project.

00:20:27.197 --> 00:20:29.422
Not two, not three, not four.

00:20:29.422 --> 00:20:32.327
Don't walk away from here without

00:20:32.327 --> 00:20:36.230
creating that list, and then prioritizing,

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:39.915
and then starting now to finish a task.

00:20:39.915 --> 00:20:44.030
You could start with small
things like starting that list.

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:45.761
If you start the list and you put

00:20:45.761 --> 00:20:48.033
four things down, guess what?

00:20:48.033 --> 00:20:50.498
You have completed your first project.

00:20:50.498 --> 00:20:53.116
Give yourself kudo and
then go into the next.

00:20:53.116 --> 00:20:54.775
It's great doing life with you.

00:20:54.775 --> 00:20:58.163
I'm encouraging you to do
something so significant

00:20:58.163 --> 00:21:00.581
that it will change your destiny,

00:21:00.581 --> 00:21:03.694
positively impact your
family, your community

00:21:03.694 --> 00:21:07.285
and an industry, and ultimately
the course of humanity.

00:21:07.285 --> 00:21:10.075
What would history be
like if it wasn't for

00:21:10.075 --> 00:21:13.340
the likes of people such
as Hans Christian Andersen

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:16.084
and Abraham Lincoln, Florence Nightingale,

00:21:16.084 --> 00:21:18.391
Christopher Columbus, the Wright brothers,

00:21:18.391 --> 00:21:21.589
Marco Polo, George Washington Carver.

00:21:21.589 --> 00:21:23.748
What would this world be like

00:21:23.748 --> 00:21:26.490
had it not been for the likes of Einstein,

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:29.829
Beethoven, Harriet Tubman, Joan of Arc,

00:21:29.829 --> 00:21:33.970
Jean King, Winnie Mandela,
Coretta Scott King.

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:36.877
These are the people like Stephen Biko

00:21:36.877 --> 00:21:39.548
who dared to make a difference.

00:21:39.548 --> 00:21:43.016
Madam Guyon and Bishop T.D. Jakes.

00:21:43.016 --> 00:21:46.183
Van Gogh, Steven Jobs and Walt Disney.

00:21:47.536 --> 00:21:49.560
What would this generation be like

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:52.701
had it not been for the
likes of Martin Luther King,

00:21:52.701 --> 00:21:57.147
Nelson Mandella, Mahatma Gandhi,
Mary the mother of Jesus.

00:21:57.147 --> 00:22:01.822
These individuals refuse
to sit insulated within

00:22:01.822 --> 00:22:05.930
the four walls of a building
or a church or a synagogue

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:08.938
just praying and wishing
the world was different.

00:22:08.938 --> 00:22:13.293
They got up and they became
the change they wanted to see.

00:22:13.293 --> 00:22:16.029
These are the people that refuse to see

00:22:16.029 --> 00:22:18.963
themselves as victims of circumstances

00:22:18.963 --> 00:22:21.084
or products of their environment.

00:22:21.084 --> 00:22:23.524
You know one of the things
I found out is this,

00:22:23.524 --> 00:22:27.761
that these people were just
ordinary in their own eyes.

00:22:27.761 --> 00:22:31.377
They did something different,
something unorthodox

00:22:31.377 --> 00:22:35.158
until they became extraordinary in ours.

00:22:35.158 --> 00:22:37.005
That's what it takes.

00:22:37.005 --> 00:22:40.705
You can not have extraordinary
without the ordinary.

00:22:40.705 --> 00:22:44.205
It takes that to do something significant.

